{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01204 - MONDO_17894",
  "verbalization": "Mitoxantrone, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a series of indications involving Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin. The evidence suggests that Mitoxantrone is used in the treatment of AML, with Gemtuzumab Ozogamicin being a common indication for this condition. The presence of Cebpa somatic mutations in AML further supports the relationship, as these mutations are associated with a more aggressive form of the disease. The integration of these pathways implies that Mitoxantrone may exert its effects through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood, potentially influencing the progression or treatment response in AML patients with Cebpa mutations. The evidence highlights a potential role of Mitoxantrone in the management of AML, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
